From: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: ls1021a-iot: disable the SoC watchdog

The WDOG1 counter runs from the 32 kHz RTC input, which is grounded on
this board, so the watchdog never expires and a hung system is never
reset. Disable it, so that /dev/watchdog is the one in the system CPLD
(image 3.0), which counts from its own 25 MHz oscillator.

Signed-off-by: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/ls/ls1021a-iot.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/ls/ls1021a-iot.dts
@@ -466,3 +466,11 @@
 &uart1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&wdog0 {
+	/*
+	 * It never counts on this board: its clock is the 32 kHz RTC input,
+	 * and the RTC ball is grounded. The system CPLD has the watchdog.
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
+};
